n calculate the correlation using  the python  so here we are on a jupiter notebook  let's see how you can use the jupyter  notebook and python to calculate the  correlation coefficient that is  pearson's correlation coefficient  so first we'll feed the data that we  have used for our excel example  let's start by importing numpy  now  in our data sheet we had the test scores  so we'll write  this co rds goes  and the scores were 95 36 58  95 36  58  97 99 42  97  99 and  42  for the duration of ours we have  6 1 3 5 6 2  6  1  three  five six  two  so we have entered both the data of  scores and ours  now to calculate the correlation  coefficient we'll use the function  corr correlation  coefficient  and will mention both the data sets  that is  scores  and us  now let's run to see if we get the same  value as in excel  so you can see we have the same value of  0.980 as our correlation coefficient and  it matches with our excel data  so in this way you can calculate the  correlation coefficient using python  that's it  we have come to an end to this tutorial  if you like this video don't forget to  subscribe to our channel and hit that  like button  thank you again and happy learning  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here

